WEBVTT

00:00:00.556 --> 00:00:02.386
Cryptography hides meaning.

00:00:02.976 --> 00:00:05.746
Steganography hides the message itself.

00:00:06.326 --> 00:00:09.576
The attacker does not even
know a message exists.

00:00:10.151 --> 00:00:11.321
Unlike cryptography,

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.801
it does not scramble the message.

00:00:14.411 --> 00:00:16.361
It just makes the message invisible.

00:00:18.256 --> 00:00:23.706
Steganography is the art and science of
hiding the existence of communication.

00:00:24.451 --> 00:00:27.761
A message is concealed
inside another medium.

00:00:28.281 --> 00:00:33.071
An image, an audio clip, a text file,
or even a network protocol.

00:00:33.581 --> 00:00:35.731
Adversaries cannot detect it.

00:00:37.356 --> 00:00:39.506
Cryptography conceals content.

00:00:40.121 --> 00:00:42.391
Steganography conceals existence.

00:00:43.146 --> 00:00:45.116
An encrypted text looks random.

00:00:45.716 --> 00:00:48.806
A stego image looks
like an ordinary image.

00:00:49.356 --> 00:00:52.966
The two goals are different,
and they are often used together.

00:00:54.656 --> 00:00:56.546
Linguistic steganography.

00:00:57.126 --> 00:01:00.856
A null cipher hides words
inside a harmless sentence.

00:01:01.491 --> 00:01:04.261
A grille reveals selected
letters through a mask.

00:01:04.896 --> 00:01:08.206
Microdots shrink a whole
page into a tiny dot.

00:01:08.711 --> 00:01:11.001
The secret hides in the wording itself.

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:14.352
Technical steganography.

00:01:15.022 --> 00:01:16.812
Invisible ink on paper.

00:01:17.427 --> 00:01:20.037
Tiny characters behind white spaces.

00:01:20.582 --> 00:01:22.652
Physical tricks, not algorithms.

00:01:23.407 --> 00:01:25.177
These are the oldest methods.

00:01:26.956 --> 00:01:28.526
Digital steganography.

00:01:29.156 --> 00:01:33.966
Least significant bit embedding
changes the last bits of image pixels.

00:01:34.611 --> 00:01:38.221
Spread spectrum spreads the
signal across a wide band.

00:01:38.771 --> 00:01:40.681
Spam can carry hidden text.

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:43.156
The secret hides in the noise.

00:01:44.922 --> 00:01:47.892
Cryptography says: read this if you can.

00:01:48.422 --> 00:01:51.472
Steganography says:
there is nothing to read.

00:01:52.022 --> 00:01:54.752
Together they give both
secrecy and stealth.

00:01:55.337 --> 00:01:56.747
That is the difference.

